  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.6\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.38 \\\\ 0.62\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.4 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.38 \\\\ 0.62\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.324 \\\\ 0.676\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
